<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91392" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πῡθώ</span></b> , gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦς</span>,
		dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῖ</span>, ἡ,
			<u>Pytho</u>, the region in which lay the city of Delphi,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πυθοῖ ἔνι πετρηέσσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.405
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Π. ἐν ἠγαθέῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.80
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				499
			</span></i>, etc.; of Delphi itself, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.66
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.54
			</span></i>, etc. (Acc. to the legend, derived from the <i>rotting</i>
			of the serpent, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				372
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
